===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂yew-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|abjuren|t=to give up (something); to recant or renounce (something) under oath}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=abjūren|pos=v|id=MED108}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|abjurer}}, {{der|en|frm|abiurer}}, {{m|frm|abjurer}}, and {{der|en|fro|abjurer|t=to reject or renounce (something) on oath}} (modern {{cog|fr|abjurer}}), and from their {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|abiūrāre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|abiūrō|t=to deny on oath, recant, renounce, repudiate, abjure}}, from {{m|la|ab-|pos={{glossary|prefx}} meaning ‘away from, from’}} + {{m|la|iūro|t=to take an oath, swear, vow}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂yew-|t=(''adjective'') right; straight; upright; (''noun'') justice; law; right}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9097270146|date=September 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

